  "visual": {
    "visualType": "textbox",
    "objects": {
      "general": [
        {
          "properties": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "About this page · The Scan",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "18pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "What this page is for",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "14pt",
                      "color": "#9cbce8"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "746 cells were scanned. 11 hold thirty people or more — below that, an attrition rate is arithmetic on too few lives to act on. 4 of those eleven trip a rule.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "The point of this page is not the four. It is the seven that do not fire, and one pair in particular. Bogotá Operations IC3 and São Paulo Sales IC3 are identical: 35 people, 8 voluntary exits against 4.7 expected, 1.69× the company baseline, p = 0.107. Neither fires. At that population an elevated reading has close to a one-in-nine chance of being noise, and this analysis will not spend a salary budget on a one-in-nine. Under the \"1.5× the baseline\" rule of thumb this rule replaced, both would have been recommended for a raise.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Dublin fires on the lowest attrition on the page. 0.74× the baseline, p = 0.854 — statistically the quietest cell here. Rule 2 catches it through the tenure split alone: incumbents at the 25th peer percentile against recent hires at the 74th. It is the only segment found before attrition reacted, which is the only time an equity correction is cheap.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "How to read the chart",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "14pt",
                      "color": "#9cbce8"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Horizontal — attrition against the company baseline. 1.0 is the company rate.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Vertical — the probability of seeing this many exits, or more, if the cell ran at the company rate. Log scale, and lower is stronger: a cell near the bottom is one whose gap is hard to explain by chance. The dashed line is α = 0.05.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Bubble size — average headcount over the trailing twelve months. Size is why the significance test matters: the same ratio on 100 people and on 35 are not the same finding.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Color — which rule fired, or pale where none did.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "The figures",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "14pt",
                      "color": "#9cbce8"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Attrition p-value ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "The one-sided Poisson probability of the observed exit count given the company rate. DAX has no Poisson function, so the exact tail is summed in logarithms against a table of ln(k!) and checked against two independent implementations in Python that agree to 1e-12.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Expected Exits LTM",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "What this cell would have produced at the company rate. It exists to be compared against the actual count and for nothing else.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "TTC ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Total target cash against market: base plus variable target, not base alone. The single most consequential choice in the rule. Base pay alone puts São Paulo Sales at 0.88 and recommends a raise for a population that was never underpaid.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Average Span of Control ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Reports per manager. What separates a pay problem from an organizational one: Singapore sits at 15.1 against 6.7 company-wide, with a compa-ratio of 1.01.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "The materiality floor ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Thirty people. A rule that cannot act below thirty has no business reporting below thirty.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
